From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:35:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: ave: expose frame-level rate control

V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FRAME_RC_ENABLE is the one control Chromium's V4L2
video encoder requires: V4L2VideoEncodeAccelerator::InitControls() sets it
to 1 and refuses the device when that fails ("This is the only mandatory
control"). The encoder has no such control, so a browser built with the
V4L2 encoder gets no hardware encoder on these Macs.

The firmware always controls the rate per frame, in every bitrate mode the
driver offers (variable bitrate and constant quality), and has no mode
without it. Offer the control with 1 as its only value, so clients that
enable rate control succeed and none can turn it off.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c
index feaf8f0e81..755e073f8e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/ave-v4l2.c
@@ -537,6 +537,7 @@ static int ave_s_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 		ctx->prioritize_speed = ctrl->val;
 		break;
 	case V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE:
+	case V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FRAME_RC_ENABLE:
 	case V4L2_CID_MIN_BUFFERS_FOR_OUTPUT:
 		break;
 	default:
@@ -565,7 +566,7 @@ static int ave_init_ctrls(struct ave_ctx *ctx)
 	const struct v4l2_ctrl_ops *ops = &ave_ctrl_ops;
 	struct v4l2_ctrl *c;
 
-	v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(hdl, 19);
+	v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(hdl, 20);
 
 	/*
 	 * The 6070 firmware path (M1 Pro/Max, M2) is qualified for constant
@@ -590,6 +591,11 @@ static int ave_init_ctrls(struct ave_ctx *ctx)
 	 * 0 means twice the average, as macOS sets it.
 	 */
 	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_BITRATE_PEAK, 0, 200000000, 1, 0);
+	/*
+	 * The firmware controls the rate per frame in every mode offered here and
+	 * has no mode without it. Chromium's V4L2 encoder requires the control.
+	 */
+	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FRAME_RC_ENABLE, 1, 1, 1, 1);
 	/* 0 means no limit; the firmware then uses 120 frames. */
 	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_GOP_SIZE, 0, 65535, 1, 30);
 	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FORCE_KEY_FRAME, 0, 0, 0, 0);
